     "title": {
      "id": "Lab: ETL tervalidasi, streaming, dan idempoten",
      "en": "Lab: a validated, streaming, idempotent ETL"
     },
     "description": {
      "id": "Bangun versi produksi dari job pembersihan di Modul 0.2. Ia membaca pesanan KopiKu yang kotor, memvalidasi tiap baris dengan model Pydantic, menulis baris baik dan baris karantina ke file terpisah, tidak pernah menahan file di memori, aman dijalankan dua kali, dan memberi sinyal sukses atau gagal lewat exit code-nya. Tesnya sudah ditulis untuk Anda, dan memeriksa perilaku (memori, eksekusi ulang, kegagalan), bukan hanya nilai.",
      "en": "Build the production version of the cleaning job from Module 0.2. It reads the dirty KopiKu orders, validates each row with a Pydantic model, writes good rows and quarantined rows to separate files, never holds the file in memory, can be run twice safely, and signals success or failure with its exit code. Tests are written for you, and they check behaviour (memory, repeat runs, failures), not just values."
     },
     "steps": {
      "id": "> **Sudah menyelesaikan Jeda Praktik 1–4?** File `labs/mod-1-2/etl.py` Anda sudah selesai, langsung lompat ke Langkah 7 untuk menjalankan verifikasi penuh dan membuat kode bukti Anda.\n\n1. Persiapan di dalam repositori kursus (Anda akan mengedit `labs/mod-1-2/etl.py`). Pasang requirement dan buat datanya:\n\n```bash\npython -m pip install -r labs/mod-1-2/requirements.txt\npython3 labs/shared/shopgen.py --out data\n```\n\n2. Baca dulu `labs/mod-1-2/test_lab.py`. Itulah spesifikasinya. Perhatikan apa yang diperiksanya: hitungan terhadap ground truth generator, memori di bawah 30 MB pada file 120.000 baris, keluaran identik byte demi byte saat dijalankan ulang, keluaran sebelumnya tetap ada saat eksekusi gagal, exit code 0, 1, dan 2.\n3. Buka `labs/mod-1-2/etl.py` dan implementasikan, dengan urutan ini, jalankan tes setelah tiap langkah:\n   `OrderRow` (constraint dan validator), lalu `validate`, lalu `read_orders` (sebuah generator), lalu `run`, lalu `main`.\n4. Di `run`, pakai pola karantina: untuk tiap baris tulis ke keluaran atau tulis `{\"row\", \"reason\", \"raw\"}` ke karantina, dan hitung yang terjadi. Susun alasan dari error validasi pertama (diawali nama field yang gagal). Lakukan pemeriksaan duplikat hanya untuk baris yang lolos validasi.\n5. Buat `run` atomik: tulis ke file `f\"{output_path}.tmp\"` dan `f\"{quarantine_path}.tmp\"` lalu `os.replace` di akhir; dalam `try/except` hapus file sementara dan lempar ulang pada kegagalan apa pun.\n6. Di `main(argv=None)`, parse `input`, `output`, `quarantine`, dan `--max-reject-rate` (default `0.05`) dengan `argparse` (teruskan `argv` ke `parser.parse_args(argv)`). Kembalikan `0` saat sukses, catat error dan kembalikan `1` bila `stats.reject_rate > args.max_reject_rate`, dan kembalikan `2` bila file input tidak bisa dibaca (`OSError`).\n7. Jalankan tes, jalankan program pada data asli (menulis ke `/tmp/` agar repositori tetap bersih), lihat karantinanya, dan buat kode bukti Anda:\n\n```bash\npytest labs/mod-1-2 -v\npython3 labs/mod-1-2/etl.py data/orders.csv /tmp/clean.ndjson /tmp/quarantine.ndjson; echo \"exit code: $?\"\nhead -3 /tmp/quarantine.ndjson\npython3 scripts/prove.py mod-1-2\n```\n\n   **Seharusnya Anda melihat** dari perintah kedua: baris log seperti `INFO read=3634 valid=3582 duplicates=35 invalid=17` dan `exit code: 0`. Lalu `wc -l /tmp/clean.ndjson` menunjukkan 3582 dan `wc -l /tmp/quarantine.ndjson` menunjukkan 52 (35 duplikat dan 17 total negatif), dan `head -3 /tmp/quarantine.ndjson` menampilkan baris berisi `raw`, `reason` (misalnya `total_idr: greater_than`), dan `row`.\n\n8. Tantangan tambahan opsional: tambahkan helper retry dan tes yang memakai `monkeypatch` untuk mensimulasikan dua kegagalan sebelum sukses; tambahkan type hint dan jalankan `mypy`.",
      "en": "> **Already completed Practice Pauses 1–4?** Your `labs/mod-1-2/etl.py` is already implemented, skip straight to Step 7 to run the full verification and generate your proof code.\n\n1. Set up inside the course repository (you will edit `labs/mod-1-2/etl.py`). Install the requirements and generate the data:\n\n```bash\npython -m pip install -r labs/mod-1-2/requirements.txt\npython3 labs/shared/shopgen.py --out data\n```\n\n2. Read `labs/mod-1-2/test_lab.py` first. It is the specification. Notice what it checks for: counts against the generator's ground truth, memory under 30 MB on a 120,000-row file, byte-identical outputs on rerun, previous output preserved when a run fails, exit codes 0, 1 and 2.\n3. Open `labs/mod-1-2/etl.py` and implement, in this order, running the tests after each step:\n   `OrderRow` (constraints and validators), then `validate`, then `read_orders` (a generator), then `run`, then `main`.\n4. In `run`, use the quarantine pattern: for each row either write it to the output or write `{\"row\", \"reason\", \"raw\"}` to the quarantine, and count what happens. Build the reason from the first validation error (starting with the failing field name). Do the duplicate check only for rows that validated.\n5. Make `run` atomic: write to `f\"{output_path}.tmp\"` and `f\"{quarantine_path}.tmp\"` and `os.replace` them at the end; in a `try/except` remove the temporary files and re-raise on any failure.\n6. In `main(argv=None)`, parse `input`, `output`, `quarantine`, and `--max-reject-rate` (default `0.05`) with `argparse` (passing `argv` to `parser.parse_args(argv)`). Return `0` on success, log an error and return `1` when `stats.reject_rate > args.max_reject_rate`, and return `2` if the input file cannot be read (`OSError`).\n7. Run the tests, run the program on the real data (writing to `/tmp/` so the repository stays clean), look at the quarantine, and generate your proof code:\n\n```bash\npytest labs/mod-1-2 -v\npython3 labs/mod-1-2/etl.py data/orders.csv /tmp/clean.ndjson /tmp/quarantine.ndjson; echo \"exit code: $?\"\nhead -3 /tmp/quarantine.ndjson\npython3 scripts/prove.py mod-1-2\n```\n\n   **You should see** from the second command: a log line like `INFO read=3634 valid=3582 duplicates=35 invalid=17` and `exit code: 0`. Then `wc -l /tmp/clean.ndjson` says 3582 and `wc -l /tmp/quarantine.ndjson` says 52 (35 duplicates and 17 negative totals), and `head -3 /tmp/quarantine.ndjson` shows lines with `raw`, `reason` (for example `total_idr: greater_than`) and `row`.\n\n8. Optional stretch goals: add a retry helper and a test that uses `monkeypatch` to simulate two failures before success; add type hints and run `mypy`."
     },
     "verify": {
      "id": "```bash\npytest labs/mod-1-2 -v\npython3 scripts/prove.py mod-1-2\n```\n\nBandingkan dengan hasil yang sudah benar: `LAB_DIR=reference pytest labs/mod-1-2 -v`. Jika tes memori gagal, kemungkinan Anda menahan semua baris sekaligus; pakai `tracemalloc` seperti di pelajaran untuk menemukan tempatnya.",
      "en": "```bash\npytest labs/mod-1-2 -v\npython3 scripts/prove.py mod-1-2\n```\n\nCompare with a known-good run: `LAB_DIR=reference pytest labs/mod-1-2 -v`. If the memory test fails, you are probably holding all rows at once; use `tracemalloc` as shown in the lesson to find where."
     },
