       "en": "A Dead-Letter Queue provides fault isolation without data loss. If an event is too late or malformed, failing the entire pipeline halts operations for all clean traffic, while silently dropping the record loses audit traceability. A DLQ quarantines defective payloads with error metadata for offline inspection and replay."
